"""Shared library module with no library-internal deps of its own.

Because the aspect-based checks in `.bazelrc` validate *every* module, not just
root modules, a library module that names a provider needs the providers hub
too (which carries the lock). That is the wrapper earning its keep: a broken shared module
fails on its own target instead of in whichever environment adopts it next.
"""

load("@rules_terraform//terraform:terraform_module.bzl", "terraform_module")

terraform_module(
    name = "storage",
    srcs = glob(["*.tf"]),
    visibility = ["//visibility:public"],
    deps = ["@shared"],
)
